c,=20
but "every" and "each" are restricted to Anglic or Low German, from what I=
=20
know. "All things" can mean "ro da" or "lu'o ro da", "each thing" is "lu'a =
ro=20
da", and I'm not sure how to explain the difference between "every" (from=
=20
ME "everich"=3D"ever each") and "each". It's the same difference as "todo"=
=20
vs. "cada".

"ma" does not have to be everything at once. It can be any one thing at a=
=20
time. If you want to ask what things broda together, you can say "lu'o ma p=
oi=20
roda cu broda".

